text: |-
  = WEARNEWS@3
  76°
  WATCH
  When Utah Gov. Spencer Cox appointed Graf
  to the 4th District Court in May, he praised him
  as someone who brings "a steady hand, strong
  ethics, and the kind of judgment we count on
  in Utah's judiciary."
  Still, no one expected his first major
  assignment would come so quickly after he
  was sworn in on Aug. 4, 2025.
  "It's not something he asked for," Evershed
  said. "It's not something anyone could have
  anticipated."
  Before becoming a judge, Graf prosecuted sex
  abuse cases in Davis County. His résumé also
  includes time leading the Special Victims Unit
  for the Utah County Attorney's Office, serving
  as an assistant attorney general in American
  Samoa, and working as a special assistant U.S.
  attorney in Washington, D.C.
